_review","pull_request_review_comment","push","registry_package","release","repository","repository_dispatch","status","watch","workflow_dispatch","workflow_run"]},"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/comments/5569264756","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/41188#issuecomment-5569264756","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/41188","id":5569264756,"node_id":"IC_kwDOOYsS4c8AAAABS_Q8dA","user":{"login":"valeriyproklov","id":99179211,"node_id":"U_kgDOBelayw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99179211?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeriyproklov","html_url":"https://github.com/valeriyproklov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeriyproklov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeriyproklov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeriyproklov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeriyproklov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeriyproklov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeriyproklov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeriyproklov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeriyproklov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/valeriyproklov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-07T10:29:31Z","updated_at":"2026-09-07T10:29:31Z","body":"Additional reproduction with Omarchy's mise-managed Codex installation:\n\n- Omarchy: 4.0.2-1\n- Platform: Linux x86_64\n- Codex CLI: 0.153.2\n- Install method: Omarchy's `omarchy-mise-install codex`; global mise configuration has `codex = \"latest\"`.\n- Resolved executable: `~/.local/share/mise/installs/codex/latest/bin/codex`.\n\nRunning `codex remote-control start` fails before the daemon starts:\n\n```text\nStarting app-server daemon with remote control enabled...\nError: managed standalone Codex install not found at <HOME>/.codex/packages/standalone/current/codex\n\nThis command requires the standalone install managed by the Codex installer, because the daemon starts and updates app-server from that fixed path.\n```\n\nThe error then recommends the standalone installer. Omarchy already owns Codex installation and updates through mise: its installed `omarchy-update-mise` script runs `MISE_MINIMUM_RELEASE_AGE=0 mise up`. Requiring another installation introduces a second update owner for the same tool.\n\nAn explicit externally managed executable setting, with daemon updates left to mise, would address this Omarchy use case as well. The desired behavior is for `codex remote-control start` to launch the mise-managed executable without requiring a synthesized standalone directory or running the standalone installer.\n\nThis report confirms the startup failure only; successful remote pairing has not been tested.\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/comments/5569264756/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/comments/5834492629","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/41188#issuecomment-5834492629","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/41188","id":5834492629,"node_id":"IC_kwDOOYsS4c8AAAABW8NK1Q","user":{"login":"etraut-openai","id":223546144,"node_id":"U_kgDODVMLIA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/223546144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/etraut-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-25T14:55:15Z","updated_at":"2026-09-25T14:55:15Z","body":"There is already a way to disable automatic daemon updates: set `updater.autoUpdateEnabled` to `false` in `$CODEX_HOME/app-server-daemon/settings.json` (normally `~/.codex/app-server-daemon/settings.json`):\n\n```json\n{\n  \"updater\": {\n    \"autoUpdateEnabled\": false\n  }\n}\n```\n\nIf the file already contains settings, add this field without removing them. Run `codex app-server daemon restart` to apply the change. This disables automatic updates; an explicit `codex app-server daemon update` can still install an update.\n\nThat setting alone doesn’t address the executable selection problem. The latest CLI can initialize a daemon by copying a complete CLI package into a separate daemon-owned directory, but that copy is independent of the package manager’s installation. A bare executable or an incompatible package layout still cannot be used this way.\n\nA possible solution is an environment variable such as `CODEX_DAEMON_EXECUTABLE` containing the path to the externally managed `codex` executable. When set, daemon start and bootstrap would launch that executable directly, skip the package copy and installer, and leave updates to the package manager. Explicit daemon update requests would report that the executable is externally managed. An invalid path would produce an actionable error; when the variable is unset, the current managed behavior would remain the default.\n\nThe wrapper or environment would need to provide the variable for each relevant Codex invocation. After the package manager updates the executable, restarting the daemon would pick up the new version.\n\nDoes that sound like it would meet your needs?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/comments/5834492629/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/comments/5968869402","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/41188#issuecomment-5968869402","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/41188","id":5968869402,"node_id":"IC_kwDOOYsS4c8AAAABY8W4Gg","user":{"login":"Lenoridev","id":122464369,"node_id":"U_kgDOB0yocQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/122464369?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenoridev","html_url":"https://github.com/Lenoridev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenoridev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenoridev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenoridev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenoridev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenoridev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenoridev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenoridev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenoridev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenoridev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-03T11:49:01Z","updated_at":"2026-10-03T11:49:01Z","body":"This also affects the official Arch Linux `openai-codex` package managed by `pacman`. After `pacman -Syu` upgrades Codex, the managed app-server under `~/.codex/packages/app-server-daemon` can remain on the previous version, so you have to manually update it through `/daemon`.\n\nFor package-manager installs, having the daemon use the externally managed executable as proposed here would avoid the duplicated update lifecycle entirely.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/comments/5968869402/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/comments/6091668448","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/41188#issuecomment-6091668448","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/41188","id":6091668448,"node_id":"IC_kwDOOYsS4c8AAAABaxd74A","user":{"login":"astral303","id":1194357,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExOTQzNTc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1194357?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/astral303","html_url":"https://github.com/astral303","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/astral303/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/astral303/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/astral303/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/astral303/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/astral303/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/astral303/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/astral303/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/astral303/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/astral303/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-10T00:34:13Z","updated_at":"2026-10-10T00:34:13Z","body":"Yes, a `CODEX_DAEMON_EXECUTABLE` would definitely meet my needs for running patched builds of Codex. I can't speak for the OP, but you have my thumbs up.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/comments/6091668448/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]